        "id": "a1",
        "title": "Finding the first sentence",
        "category": "Writing Notes",
        "date": "2025-05-18",
        "excerpt": "A few thoughts on patience, observation and beginning before every idea feels ready.",
        "content": "The first sentence rarely arrives as a finished thing. More often, it appears as a question, an image or a small detail worth following. Writing begins when we give that detail enough room to become a story.",
